[anyone|plyr,"final_player_21",[
  (quest_slot_ge, "qst_freelancing", slot_quest_freelancer_rank, 2),
],"Shut up and hear me! I can't stand this madness anymore.^I've dedicated years in service to Rome, witnessing the brutality of death, torture, and rape. I endured my share of suffering, all in the name of Rome's glory."
+" When I was finally invited to the palace, the truth unraveled - the Rome we fought for was nothing more than a congregation of self-serving, obsessed, vain, beautiful, arrogant, proud, and megalomaniacal individuals."
+" This revelation made motivating my soldiers a challenge; how could I ask them to risk their lives for a corrupt and decadent Rome? Despite the struggle,"
+" I vowed to purify this tainted seat of power, to resurrect its former glory.",
"final_antonia_3",[]],

[anyone|plyr,"final_player_21",[
  (neg|quest_slot_ge, "qst_freelancing", slot_quest_freelancer_rank, 2),
],"Shut up and hear me! I can't stand this madness anymore.^After years of relentless toil, I have ascended to the echelons of nobility through unwavering determination. Yet, as I gaze upon the opulence surrounding me, a disquieting truth unfolds"
+" - the corruption that stains the very core of Rome and plagues the majority of the nobility. In the pursuit of prosperity, I have climbed a ladder only to discover that it leans against a wall of deceit and decay."
+" It's time to uphold the values that Rome was built upon, and to restore Roman honor. The wealth I have amassed should not be a testament to silent complicity, but a catalyst for change."
+" For the sake of Rome's glory and legacy I will strive to redeem the noble ideals of Rome that have been tarnished by the very hands that should protect them.",
"final_antonia_3",[]],

[anyone|other(trp_antonia),"final_antonia_3",[
],"--Silence ensues. After a brief moment, Antonia speaks.--^^Let's continue, {playername}, with our judgment. Tigellinus: You are an arsonist, thus you are punished to burn alive!",
"final_tigellinius_10",[
  (call_script, "script_set_conversation_troop", "trp_antonia"),
]],

[anyone|other(trp_tigellinus),"final_tigellinius_10",[
],"Let me forewarn you {playername}: your path as Caesar will not be strewn with ease. I find myself almost relieved at the prospect of departing from this tumultuous world.",
"final_player_23",[
  (call_script, "script_set_conversation_troop", "trp_tigellinus"),
]],

[anyone|plyr,"final_player_23",[
],"Nero! Now to you!",
"final_nero_14",[]],

[anyone|other(trp_kingdom_7_lord),"final_nero_14",[
],"Has anyone ever inquired if I aspired to don the mantle of Caesar? Never! If it were within my sway, I'd have chosen the path of a poet, but Fortuna had divergent designs for my fate."
+" I persistently sought to pacify the masses. Can I be held accountable for the fact that my company often comprised power-hungry serpents? Is it my culpability that the Roman aristocracy spurned my art?"
+" Should I bear the blame for their concerted efforts to garner opposition, asserting a Caesar ought not to indulge in song and dance?",
"final_antonia_3_1",[
  (call_script, "script_set_conversation_troop", "trp_kingdom_7_lord"),
]],

[anyone|other(trp_antonia),"final_antonia_3_1",[
],"Nero, do you possess a will independent of others? Who truly governed Rome? Was it Agrippina, Seneca, Poppaea, or Tigellinus? Certainly not Nero! It's a stark truth: no one solicits our aspirations."
+" However, you had the opportunity to shape your destiny more positively. You could have heeded voices like Seneca's over the braying of individuals like Tigellinus."
+" Poetry could have been your solace, and it wouldn't have inconvenienced anyone. Yet, the belief that you were the paramount artist, compelling applause and punishing dissent, that incited both ire and repulsion among all!",
"final_nero_15",[
  (call_script, "script_set_conversation_troop", "trp_antonia"),
]],

[anyone|other(trp_kingdom_7_lord),"final_nero_15",[
  ],
"--He weeps, collapsing to the ground in an emotional upheaval..--^^Please, please, gracious {playername}, gracious Antonia. I implore you, spare my life, unlike the fate Tigellinus faced! Instead, consider banishing me to a distant island or some remote exile. There, I could exist in peace, dedicating my days to crafting poems, plays, and weaving tales as I have always yearned. I beseech you, oh benevolent one! If blood must be spilled, let it be Poppaea's and Tigellinus's, but spare me from such a grim end!",
"final_poppaea_11",[
  (call_script, "script_set_conversation_troop", "trp_kingdom_7_lord"),
]],

