[trp_aux_commander_new_6|plyr,"lord_talk",[
    (troop_slot_eq, "trp_global_variables", g_germanicus_intro, 0),
 ],
    "I heard you served under Germanicus when he campaigned East of the Rhine.",
    "germanicus_talk",[
      (troop_set_slot, "trp_global_variables", g_germanicus_intro, 1),
  ]],

[anyone,"germanicus_talk",[
 ],
    "That is true! After Augstus death, the Rhine legions revolted. Germanicus paid them from his own pocket to restore order and then led them to raid the Germanic tribe of the Marsi."
    +" We destroyed many of their villages. We also raided villages and forts of the Bructeri, Tubantes and Usipetes, killing many of their people."
    +" For the next years he led the legions across the Rhine to confront Arminius and his allies, taking revenge for the cursed battle."
    +" We sacked the capital of the Chatti and we capture Arminius' wife Thusnelda. Arminius mobilized his tribes."
    +" Using the Rhine as supply line, we coordinated a massive attack on the Arminius hordes. At that time Lucius Stertinius recovered the lost eagle of the XIX legion.",
    "germanicus_talk_2",[
  ]],
#
[anyone,"germanicus_talk_2",[
 ],
    "We also found the left overs of the Varus battle and began burying the bones. We had finally a battle with Arminius, but unfortunately he escaped."
    +" That marked the end of the third Germanic campaign. We prepared forces for a third campaign and finally crossed the Rhine again."
    +" Finally, we could catch Arminius: We slaughtered his forces on the plains of Idistaviso. Though the rat Arminius was able to escape."
    +" Interestingly we took no prisioners at all. Germanicus decided its not worth it. He said the extermination of the Germanic tribes was the only conclusion he saw for the war."
    +" An opinion that I still share. But anyhow, in total I would call the campaigns a great success. We restored two of the three lost eagles, we defeated Arminius and we punished them by slaughtering thousands and thousands of warriors, women and children.",
    "germanicus_talk_3",[
  ]],

[anyone|plyr,"germanicus_talk_3",[],
  "Also rumours say you murdered Caligula?",
"germanicus_talk_3_2",[]],

[anyone,"germanicus_talk_3_2",[],
  "Caligula... By that time I was Prefect of the Praetorian guard... Whenever I had to kiss Caligula's ring he hold out his hand to kiss, forming and moving it in an obscene fashion."
  +" He also forced us to use degrading watch-words at night, like 'Venus', which was a slang for a male eunuch by that time. We also had to use the word 'Priapus', which is a minor god depicted with an erected phallus."
  +" Pff. That was disgusting, in many ways simply disgusting... but anyway, coming back to your question: It is obvious that the Praetorians have a certain influence on the Princeps."
  +" I saw it as my duty for Rome to act and get ride of this maniac. Which means: The rumours are true, I ordered his death. I don't have to be afraid to admit it, nobody ever liked Caligula.",
"germanicus_talk_3",[]],

[anyone|plyr,"germanicus_talk_3",[],
  "You think the total extinction of the Germanic people is the only way to pacify them. Why not Romanizing them in the usual was?",
"germanicus_talk_3_1",[]],

[anyone,"germanicus_talk_3_1",[],
  "We tried that at first, but it failed and was very costly! At the end, a total of three legions was destroyed. I think we shouldn't waste our time with retrying failed efforts."
  +" And that's why Germanicus took no prisoners and that's why I share his opinion. I am also never taking Germanic prisioners. However, conquering Germania is not worth it at all."
  +" It's a large forest area without any valuable goods.",
"germanicus_talk_3",[]],

[anyone|plyr,"germanicus_talk_3",[],
  "Very interesting. Thank you for answering my questions.",
"lord_pretalk",[]],

