[anyone, "gartnait_historia",[(le, "$g_talk_troop_relation", 5)],
"How? That's not important.", "lord_pretalk",[]],
[anyone, "gartnait_historia",[],
"What? -- His eyes widen. -- As you know, they are ritual paintings, {playername}.", "gartnait_talk1",[]],

[anyone|plyr, "gartnait_talk1",[],
"I'd like to know why they painted their bodies and how I can get the same.", "gartnait_historia1",[]],
[anyone|plyr, "gartnait_talk1",[],
"Thanks.", "lord_pretalk",[]],

[anyone, "gartnait_historia1",[],
"We ave many ancient traditions. Young warriors are expected to paint their bodies and join the fray of battle and war before they are accepted in their homes as full-grown men. " +
"Women have the right to choose wives for their brothers, and children inherit through their mothers' lineage.^^" +
"Painting our bodies and joining warrior brotherhoods is part of a tradition in which young people must pass some tests in order to reach maturity. Some tests still involve venturing into distant lands in search of cattle and treasures, then to come home with enough wealth to start a family.",
"gartnait_historia2",[]],

[anyone, "gartnait_historia2",[],
"When the young people return, the war paint is removed from their bodies, and they marry and integrate into regular society. " +
# "There are not a few Pictish women who decide to paint their bodies to participate in this test of initiation.^^-- He smiles. -- " +
"It's up to you whether to paint your body or not. If you do, you devote yourself to a very old tradition and to powers that are beyond our understanding. " +
"Form or join a group of young people. Make a name for yourselves. Learn the camaraderie, friendship, and pride of being a Pict. Learn to command and obey. Gain the respect of your peers. When you've proven your worth, remove the war paint and return to society.",
"gartnait_historia3",[]],

[anyone|plyr, "gartnait_historia3",[],
"Stop. Your story is prattle. You are a bunch of idiots.",
"lord_pretalk",[
  (call_script, "script_troop_change_relation_with_troop", "$g_talk_troop", "trp_player", -10),
]],
[anyone|plyr, "gartnait_historia3",[],
"Thanks for the information.",
"lord_pretalk",[]],

[trp_statthalter_new_6|plyr,"lord_talk",[
  (troop_slot_eq, "$g_talk_troop", slot_troop_intro, 0),
],"I heard you defeated the rebellion of the Britannic queen Boudica.",
"sueton_talk_1",[]],

[anyone,"sueton_talk_1",[
],"Yes. I was campaigning against rebell strongholds in the North of Britannia. Then I got news that Iceni revolted against our rule, lead by their queen Boudica."
+" They clearly drew inspiration from Arminius rebellion. However, those savages started to loot and raid Britannia. They completly destroyed Camulodunum."
+" That's what they call freedom: Killing and looting towns and villages. They then advanced towards Londinium. I was outnumbered and decided to regroup. For this I had to sacrifice Londinium. Unfortunately, but it was necessary."
+" They looted Londinium and tortured the remaining population. While they raided, I regrouped my forces. I had Legio Gemina and Legio Valeria Victrix under command."
+" I managed to get Boudica into a final battle. Although outnumbered we slaughtered the savages. Boudica was driving on her chariot and leading her troops."
" But she managed to escape with her chariot. She later killed herself. A weak coward, but what to expect from a Barbarian woman?",
"lord_pretalk",[
  (troop_set_slot, "$g_talk_troop", slot_troop_intro, 1),
]],

[trp_statthalter_new_7|plyr,"lord_talk",[
  (troop_slot_eq, "$g_talk_troop", slot_troop_intro, 0),
],"I heard you warned about the uprising of the Iceni in Britannia.",
"classicianus_talk_1",[]],

[anyone,"classicianus_talk_1",[
],"Indeed. I expressed multiple concerns that the harsh politic of Suetonius who was governor of Britannia by that time would lead to an uprising sooner or later."
+" I believe its better to Romanize a province peacefully, everything else will just cause unnecessary bloodsheed.",
"lord_pretalk",[
  (troop_set_slot, "$g_talk_troop", slot_troop_intro, 1),
]],

