[anyone, "greeks_talk_christ",
[],
  "This religion is basically a sect of Judaism and was founded some decades ago when a man, called Jesus Christus, was crucified. They believe he is the messiah. The one for which the Jews are waiting for centuries.^I must say, What they believe may seem to be pleasant to a lot of people, especially poor. They preach total equality, in particular, that there is no difference between rich and poor, a Caesar and a slave. That sounds good for slaves, beggars and other poor folk. I also heard they believe that death is start of a new eternal life. And for me, this all sounds like an attempt of escape: Imaging, you are a slave. You know you will be a slave for the rest of your life. Then there comes a man who tells you: Well you are good, the way you life is good. The others, who enslaved you, your masters, are bad, worse the worst. They will be punished by an almighty God. For me this sounds like an attempt of the slave to gloss over his terrible situation. But what I also noticed: This religion would be ideal to control the plebs: Since it forbids violence and to love even your enemies, no slave would ever revolt, as they are not allowed. On the other hand, why should they even revolt? One could tell them it is either a part of the plan of their God, or that they will find salvation and an eternal life after death anyway.", "greeks_talk_christ2",
[
  ]],

