[anyone|plyr, "petition4",
[],
  "No this is a bad idea.", "dip_talk33",
[]],
[anyone|plyr, "dip_talk",
[],
  "Can you tell me more about judiciary of the Empire.", "jus_talk",
[]],
[anyone, "jus_talk",[],
  "Of course. First of all, the Imperium Romanum has still many elements from the Res Publica. This elements are institutions like the senate, or offices like the consulship."
  +" Public offices act according to the principle 'Mos maiorum', the custom of the fathers. The 'Mos maiorum' is not documented. The political traditions are given from the fathers to their sons."
  +" But the Empire consists of many different cultures, people from those cultures are called peregrini. Each culture with it's own laws and tradition. The Empire treat them different, depending on the situation.",
"jus_talk2",[]],

[anyone, "jus_talk2",
[],
  "Now I will talk about the private law. As I said before, the different cultures of the Empire have different laws, this also affect private matters. The most privileges have citizens with the civitas Romana"
  +".They are considered as full citizens of Rome. Someone gain the civitas Romana through birth, or get it awarded. In contrast to the constitution, the civitas Romana is documented. But the 'Mos maiorum'"
  +" is also in terms of private law an important principle.",
"jus_talk3",[]],

[anyone|plyr, "jus_talk3",
[],
  "Tell me more about the 'civitas Romana'.", "jus_talk_civitas",
[]],
[anyone, "jus_talk_civitas",
[],
  "The civitas Romana is the summary of all privileges a true Roman citizen has. This privileges are the ius suffragiorum, this is the right to vote in the comitia, the convention. Then the ius honorum, that allows the eligibility to state offices."
  +" The ius commercii regulates law of obligations, property law and inheritance. The ius gentium regulates the transactions with peregrini. The ius conubii allows citizens to marry, and there are many other things, which I forgott.",
"jus_talk3",[]],

[anyone|plyr, "jus_talk3",
[],
  "Tell me more about the senate.", "jus_talk_senate",
[]],
[anyone, "jus_talk_senate",
[],
  "Although the old times of the Republic are gone, the Roman Senate has still an important role. As you know, the Princeps can issue edicts, those edicts have the status of a law. But to issue an edict, the Princeps must bring the proposal before the senate."
  +" Then the senators vote. If the proposal passes, a new edict is issued. If not, the Princeps can say: 'Who cares about the senate?' and issue the edict nevertheless. But it will hurt the reputation and the right to rule of the Princeps.",
"jus_talk3",[]],

[anyone|plyr, "jus_talk3",
[],
  "Thanks for that information.", "dip_talk33",
[]],
[anyone|plyr, "dip_talk",
[],

  "How does Roman politic work?", "polit_talk",
[]],
[anyone, "polit_talk",
[],
  "Well, it is quite easy. The most important thing is your relation with Rome. If Rome hates you, it could rebel, and it is very bad for your reputation if Rome turns against the Princeps. Another thing is the senat."
  +" The senat is not as important as it was during the time of the Republic. You can use the senate to improve your relation with Rome and also to lower your controversy, it is worth visiting the senate once a month or so.",
"polit_talk2",[]],

[anyone, "polit_talk2",
[],
  "Another important thing are edicts and laws. You, as Princeps, can issue edicts for certain cities or for the whole Empire. With these edicts you can manage your Empire."
  +" Another important point I should mention: As Princeps you should visit Rome regularly and stay here for some time, so that you can deal with political matters.",
"dip_talk",[]],

[anyone|plyr, "dip_talk",
[],
  "Nothing at all.", "close_window",
[]],

