###delphi talk with lykos
[trp_lykos, "start",[],
  "Welcome pilgrim who seek counsel. You are here in Delphi and I am sure you want to ask the oracle.",
"lykos_talk",[]],

[anyone, "lykos_pretalk",[],
  "Anything else, consultant?",
"lykos_talk",[]],

[anyone|plyr, "lykos_talk",[
],"Can you tell me more about Pythia and Delphi?",
"lykos_talk_delphi",[]],
[anyone, "lykos_talk_delphi",[],
"According to the myth, Zeus had two eagles fly from each end of the world, meeting in Delphi. Since then, this place is the center of the world. But I will tell you the whole myth: Gaia the mother of the earth united with the mud and gave birth to Python, a snake. Python was able to see into the future.",
"lykos_talk_delphi2",[]],

[anyone, "lykos_talk_delphi2",[],
"This snake Python lived here, where today's Delphi lies. Hera the wife of Zeus was a daughter of Gaia. Gaia foretold her that Leto, the lover of Zeus, will give birth to two children much better then hers. Hera is jeaulos\
so she ordered Python to kill Leto. But Zeus avoided this murder. Thus, Leto gave birth to Apollon and Artemis. Apollon took revenge on Python and killed the beast.\
The blood of Python transfered the ability to foretell to the grounds of Delphi.",
"lykos_talk_delphi3",[]],

[anyone, "lykos_talk_delphi3",[],
"Today, the gods speak through a priestess, the Pythia. The Pythia is a woman. Long time ago, she was the most beautiful virgin from Delphi, but then an incident happend.",
"lykos_talk_delphi4_1",[]],

[anyone, "lykos_talk_delphi4_1",[],
"It is said that, Echecrates the Thessalian, having arrived at the shrine and beheld the virgin who uttered the oracle, became enamoured of her because of her beauty, carried her away and violated her. Then the Delphians, because of this deplorable occurrence, passed a law that in the future a virgin should no longer prophesy but that an elderly woman of fifty would declare the Oracles\
and that she would be dressed in the costume of a virgin, as a sort of reminder of the prophetess of olden times.",
"lykos_talk_delphi4",[]],

[anyone, "lykos_talk_delphi4",[],
"Anyway. When the Pythia dies, her successor is determined by the gods. But the woman must be from the local area."
+" Being the Pythia is a respectable career for Greek women. Priestesses enjoy many liberties and rewards for their social position,"
+" such as freedom from taxation, the right to own property and attend public events, a salary and housing provided by the state, a wide range of duties depending on their affiliation, and often gold crowns.",
"lykos_pretalk",[]],

[anyone|plyr, "lykos_talk",[],
"What is your job?",
"lykos_talk_lykos",[]],

[anyone, "lykos_talk_lykos",[],
"I am one of the two priests of Apollon. I am responsible for the pilgrims and I organize the rituals.",
"lykos_pretalk",[]],

[anyone|plyr, "lykos_talk",[],
"I want to ask questions to Pythia.", "lykos_pythia",[]],

[anyone, "lykos_pythia",[
  (party_slot_ge, "p_delphi", slot_donate_party, 1),
],
  "Sorry, but have consulted the oracle in this month before. You must wait till next month.",
"lykos_pretalk",[]],

[anyone, "lykos_pythia",[
  (this_or_next|is_between, "$g_cur_month", 1, 3),
  (eq, "$g_cur_month", 11),
 ],
   "Sorry, consultant, but the oracle is only open in warm months and we have winter. This is because Apollo has deserted his temple. Come back in spring.",
"lykos_pretalk",[]],

[anyone, "lykos_pythia",[],
    "Very good. But before we start, you must pay the costs for the ritual. It would cost you 1000 denarii.",
"player_reaction_pythia",[]],

[anyone|plyr, "player_reaction_pythia",[
  (store_troop_gold, ":gold","trp_player"),
  (ge, ":gold", 1000),
],
    "Well, here you have 1000 denarii.",
"pythia_begin",[
  (troop_remove_gold, "trp_player", 1000)
]],

[anyone, "pythia_begin",[],
  "Then we will begin with the rituals. Come with me.",
"close_window",[
	(jump_to_menu, "mnu_pythia"),
	(finish_mission),
]],

[anyone|plyr, "player_reaction_pythia",[],
    "Let me think about it.",
"lykos_pretalk",[]],

[anyone|plyr, "lykos_talk",[],
    "Farewell.",
"close_window",[]],

