[trp_centurio_west,"start",[
  (eq, "$talk_context", tc_freelancer_event_2),
],
"(You entered the tent. It seems there is currently a debate going on. The others have noticed you but continue their discussion.)^^So you're saying the only way to govern people is through fear and violence? Did I understand you correctly?", "event_strategy_talk_1",[
(set_conversation_speaker_troop,"$temp2"),##legatus speaks not centurio
]],

[anyone,"event_strategy_talk_1",[
##now centurio speaks
],
"Not exactly Legate. What I meant was that, if people revolt, one should crush this revolt with violence.\
 But let me explain it more in detail since you can not simply kill everybody. In fact, one should use violence with care.\
 There is always a reason why people rebel. The important thing is to find that reason, and then destroy it.", "event_strategy_talk_2",[]],
[anyone|other(trp_quest_primus_pilus),"event_strategy_talk_2",[
#now this guy
],
"I am not quite sure what you mean. Could you give us an example.", "event_strategy_talk_3",[
(call_script, "script_set_conversation_troop", "trp_quest_primus_pilus"),
]],
[anyone|other(trp_quest_centurio_primus),"event_strategy_talk_3",[
#now this guy
],
"Yes, an example would be good.", "event_strategy_talk_4",[
  (call_script, "script_set_conversation_troop", "trp_quest_centurio_primus"),
]],
[anyone,"event_strategy_talk_4",[

],
"Very well. Let us consider Judea. Why should they rebel there? One might say: The taxes are too high. But if Judea would be independent, they would have to pay taxes to their king too.\
 One might say: The governor is corrupt. The people are sick of this corrupt system. But if Judea would be independent, their king might also be corrupt.\
 So why are the people in Judea so unhappy and rebellious? It seems, all they have under Roman rule they could also have under the rule of a Judean king.", "event_strategy_talk_5",[
#(set_conversation_speaker_troop,"$temp2"),##legatus speaks this line
]],
[anyone|plyr,"event_strategy_talk_5",[],
"Nobody likes to be ruled by a foreign power. They are proud people after all.", "event_strategy_talk_5_2",
[]],

[anyone,"event_strategy_talk_5_2",[],
"That is true in a way but it is more complicated. The commoners are idiots after all, if you give them everything they need to live they are usually happy.\
 But there are also Judean nobles and priests who would like to rule Judea independently. Their priests are constantly preaching \
 against Rome and against Caesar.", "event_strategy_talk_6",[]],

[anyone|plyr,"event_strategy_talk_5",[],
"Their priests spur them.", "event_strategy_talk_5_1",[
 (val_add, "$temp1", 1),
]],

[anyone,"event_strategy_talk_5_1",[],
"Exactly!", "event_strategy_talk_6",[]],

[anyone|plyr,"event_strategy_talk_5",[],
"-- Listen to the conversation. --", "event_strategy_talk_6",[]],

[anyone,"event_strategy_talk_6",[],
"Their priests are the real problem. They want to rule over Judea without Roman interference.\
 Thats why they incite riots. The only way one could rule over Judea would be to get rid of the priests.", "event_strategy_talk_7",[]],
[anyone|other(trp_quest_centurio_primus),"event_strategy_talk_7",[],
"Don't forget the religious aspects. I don't know much about their god, but it seems its a jealous god who doesn't tolerate other gods.\
 Also the people of Judea are strong in their faith. If you would slaughter their priests they would right away revolt.",
 "event_strategy_talk_8",[(call_script, "script_set_conversation_troop", "trp_quest_centurio_primus"),]],

[anyone|plyr,"event_strategy_talk_8",[],
"Why not giving them more local autonomy?", "event_strategy_talk_8_player_autonomy",[]],

[anyone|plyr,"event_strategy_talk_8",[],
"One would have to somehow 'bribe' them", "event_strategy_talk_8_player",[(val_add, "$temp1", 1),]],

[anyone|plyr,"event_strategy_talk_8_player",[],
"If one could get the priests on his side, one could rule over Judea without the fear of revolts.", "event_strategy_talk_9",[]],

[anyone|plyr,"event_strategy_talk_8",[],
"-- Listen to the conversation. --", "event_strategy_talk_8_ai",[]],

[anyone|other(trp_quest_primus_pilus),"event_strategy_talk_8_ai",[],
"If one could get the priests on his side, one could rule over Judea without the fear of revolts.",
"event_strategy_talk_9",[(call_script, "script_set_conversation_troop", "trp_quest_primus_pilus"),]],

[anyone,"event_strategy_talk_8_player_autonomy",[
],
"Even more autonomy? Bah! We already had that decades ago and it didn't worked. Anyhow, lets assume now Judea revolts. How would you crush a revolt?", "event_strategy_talk_10",[]],

[anyone,"event_strategy_talk_9",[
],
"I get the point. But I am sure this isn't that easy as it may sounds. Anyhow, lets assume now Judea revolts. How would you crush a revolt?",
"event_strategy_talk_10",[
(call_script, "script_set_conversation_troop", "$temp2"),
]],

[anyone|plyr,"event_strategy_talk_10",[],
"Why not just let them be? Does Rome need more provinces?", "event_strategy_talk_11_no",[]],

[anyone,"event_strategy_talk_11_no",[],
"First of all, its a strategic important region. Secondly, its Rome's destiny to rule over the world. You, as true Roman, should remember this.", "event_strategy_talk_10_1",[]],

[anyone|plyr,"event_strategy_talk_10",[],
"Crush the revolt with use of violence.", "event_strategy_talk_11",[(val_add, "$temp1", 1),]],

[anyone|plyr,"event_strategy_talk_10",[],
"-- Listen to the conversation. --", "event_strategy_talk_10_1",[]],

[anyone,"event_strategy_talk_10_1",[],
"I would say one could crush the revolt with use of violence.", "event_strategy_talk_11",[]],

[anyone,"event_strategy_talk_11",[],
"And then? The people will remember it and will call it a 'crime'. This will be a good reason for a new revolt.\
 Of course you must reconquer Judea. One can not tolerate such an action. But the question is: How? What is the best way to reconquer a rebellious province?", "event_strategy_talk_12",[
(set_conversation_speaker_troop,"$temp2"),##legatus speaks not centurio
]],

[anyone|plyr,"event_strategy_talk_12",[],
"I would try to give them more autonomy and ensure competent people govern them.", "event_strategy_talk_13_no",[]],

[anyone|other(trp_quest_primus_pilus),"event_strategy_talk_13_no",[],
"Yes, Rome needs also good governors. But, as we discussed already, sooner or later they will revolt, because of their nobility and priests. I even think giving them local autonomy would make the problem even larger, as their nobility would become more powerful.",
"event_strategy_talk_12_ai",[(call_script, "script_set_conversation_troop", "trp_quest_primus_pilus"),]],

[anyone|plyr,"event_strategy_talk_12",[],
"One could enslave the whole population and then replace them with loyal people. For example the veterans.", "event_strategy_talk_13",[(val_add, "$temp1", 1),]],

[anyone|plyr,"event_strategy_talk_12",[],
"-- Listen to the conversation. --", "event_strategy_talk_12_ai",[]],

[anyone,"event_strategy_talk_12_ai",[],
"I am sure, to finally pacify the region one would have to enslave the whole population and then replace them with loyal people. For example veterans.", "event_strategy_talk_13",[]],

[anyone,"event_strategy_talk_13",[],
"Roma invicta! Caesar did something similar in Gaul. Probably this is the best way. Anyway, we have talked enough about this matter. Soldier {playername}, what have you to say?", "event_strategy_talk_14",[
(call_script, "script_set_conversation_troop", "$temp2"),
]],
[anyone|plyr,"event_strategy_talk_14",[],
"I bring a report for my Centurio, Dominus.", "event_strategy_talk_15",[(val_add, "$temp1", 1),]],
[anyone|plyr,"event_strategy_talk_14",[],
"I bring a report for my Centurio.", "event_strategy_talk_15",[]],

[anyone,"event_strategy_talk_15",[],
"Ah yes. Very good. The meeting is now over. Everyone back to duty.", "close_window",[
    (call_script, "script_change_player_relation_with_troop", "$temp2", "$temp1"),
    (val_mul, "$temp1", 2),
    (call_script, "script_freelancer_add_progress", "$temp1"),
    (call_script, "script_set_conversation_troop", "$temp2"),##legatus speaks not centurio
    (finish_mission),
    (jump_to_menu, "mnu_auto_return_map"),
]],

